     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># Prepare the data and library</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>rm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ls</span><span style=\"color:#660\">())</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>probgrp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;probgrp.txt&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Show the default ordering (alphanumerically)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sort</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">character</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">probgrp$ItemValue</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Re-ordering it save as ItemValue2. This might be what you want.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>probgrp$ItemValue2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">probgrp$ItemValue</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> levels</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">probgrp$ItemValue</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Plot the figure</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">probgrp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">ItemValue2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Probability</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  geom_line</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;darkred&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><br>On Wednesday, 24 September 2014 07:30:55 UTC+1, <a rel=\"nofollow\">cy5...@gmail.com</a>  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">原本即是 factor type 也已按所欲次序排列，但如您所說，ggplot 會自動再排序一次。因此，該如何不讓ggplot再行排序，是我想問的問題。Thanks.<br><br>ChungKai Sun於 2014年9月24日星期三UTC+8上午4時14分14秒寫道：<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">你如果把 itemValue 變成factor type, 然後把你想要的levels 順序定義好, 那ggplot 就會照著你要的順序. <div>不然, ggplot default 會把itemValue變成factor with default levels. Default levels 是照 sort(as.character(x)).<br><br>On Tuesday, September 23, 2014 1:48:17 AM UTC-7, <a rel=\"nofollow\">cy5...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">請問如何讓 ggplot 不將 x 軸的資料排序後顯示 (請參考附圖)。<div>原始資料與指令如下:</div><div><br></div><div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:227pt\" width=\"303\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n <colgroup><col style=\"width:227pt\" width=\"303\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.95pt;width:227pt\" height=\"21\" width=\"303\">probgrp</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">   item   ItemValue   Probability</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">1     1         1~49        0.1255</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">2     2      49~66.8      0.1306</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">3     3      66.8~79      0.1516</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.95pt\" height=\"21\">\